IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eta-liability-enforcement`

-- Electronic Transactions Act 2010, ss 16R, 23, 25, 26, 28 to 36 and 39 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or the regulations under the Act (none were retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_eta.py). Expected results were written
-- by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

`an ISP carrying a user's post, sued for defamation or other liability for publishing the material` MEANS NSPCase WITH
    `is a network service provider` IS TRUE
    `merely provides access to the material` IS TRUE
    `the provider has effective control over the person who supplied the material` IS FALSE
    `the basis of liability` IS `defamation or other liability for publishing the material`

`an ISP carrying a user's post, sued for infringement of rights in the material other than copyright` MEANS NSPCase WITH
    `is a network service provider` IS TRUE
